---
import Entry from "../../../layouts/Entry.astro";
import { loadObservations, observationEditionHref } from "../../../lib/observations";
import { countryObservationFacts, countryMissingFacts, observationCoverageAnchor } from "../../../lib/observation-view";
import ObservationFact from "../../../components/ObservationFact.astro";
import ObservationRefs from "../../../components/ObservationRefs.astro";
import "../../../styles/observations.css";
import { url } from "../../../lib/site";
export function getStaticPaths() {
  const { countries } = loadObservations();
  return countries.countries.map((country) => ({
    params: { code: country.id.toLowerCase() },
    props: { country },
  }));
}
const { country } = Astro.props;
const { countries, projection } = loadObservations();
const facts = countryObservationFacts(projection, country.id);
const missing = countryMissingFacts(projection,country.id);
---

<Entry
  title={`${country.name}: country data`}
  eyebrow="Country data profiles"
  summary={`${country.region} · World Bank statistical snapshot. Local interpretation remains open for coauthors.`}
  crumbs={[
    { label: "Record", href: "/record/" },
    { label: "Country profiles", href: "/record/country-profiles/" },
    { label: country.name },
  ]}
  sources={countries.indicators.map((i) => ({
    title: i.label,
    url: i.url,
    publisher: "World Bank World Development Indicators and original producers",
  }))}
>
  <p>
    This page describes national indicators. It does not identify the best
    charity, estimate the impact of a gift or speak for people living here. A
    locally authored narrative profile has not been published.
  </p>
  <h2>What the snapshot records</h2>
  <div class="ob-grid">
    {
      countries.indicators.map((i) => {
        const fact = facts[i.id];
        return (
          <>
            {fact ? <ObservationFact projection={projection} observation={fact.record} showEntity={false}/> : <article class="ob-fact" data-coverage-id={missing[i.id]?.coverage.id} data-coverage-version={missing[i.id]?.coverage.version} data-coverage-hash={missing[i.id]?.coverage.hash} data-cell-index={missing[i.id]?.index} data-edition-id={projection.edition.id} data-edition-hash={projection.edition.hash}><h3>{i.label}</h3><p><strong>Unknown in the 2020–2025 snapshot</strong></p><p>The producer returned null throughout the selection window. This is not a measured zero.</p><p>{i.note}</p>{missing[i.id]&&<><ObservationRefs projection={projection} refs={missing[i.id].cell.sourceRefs}/><details><summary>Missing-cell identity</summary><p>Coverage {missing[i.id].coverage.id} v{missing[i.id].coverage.version}, cell {missing[i.id].index}; edition {projection.edition.id}.</p><p class="ob-hash">Coverage hash {missing[i.id].coverage.hash} · edition hash {projection.edition.hash}</p></details><a href={url(`${observationEditionHref(projection.edition.id)}#${observationCoverageAnchor(missing[i.id].coverage.id,missing[i.id].coverage.version,missing[i.id].index)}`)}>Read this exact missing-coverage cell and its source</a></>}</article>}
          </>
        );
      })
    }
  </div>
  <p class="note">
    Retrieved {countries.retrieved}. Each series uses its latest non-empty
    observation in 2020–2025; the years can differ. National averages may hide
    differences by region, wealth, gender, disability or other circumstances.
    These figures do not measure charitable funding or unmet need.
  </p>
  <p><a href={url(observationEditionHref(projection.edition.id))}>Fixed observation edition {projection.edition.sequence}</a> · captured {projection.capturedAt}. The source/reuse detail belongs to each source; no blanket license or independent local review is implied.</p>
  <h2>Build an accountable local profile</h2><ol>
    <li>
      Invite local coauthors to define priorities and correct the framing.
    </li><li>
      Compare national figures with local statistical publications and
      community-led evidence.
    </li><li>
      Map public, philanthropic and informal resources separately. Record dates,
      coverage and unknown amounts.
    </li><li>
      Ask who decides, whose experience is missing and how people can safely
      challenge the work.
    </li><li>
      Publish disagreements and source limits alongside the narrative. Obtain
      independent review.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    <a class="btn" href={url(`/record/country-profiles/#country=${country.id}`)}
      >Compare data and write a research brief</a>
  </p>
  <h2>Where work may act</h2><p>
    For a water question, for example, emergency supply can provide relief;
    infrastructure repairs can restore service; maintenance and treatment can
    prevent interruptions; utility rules and accountability can change
    structures; and coordination or shared information may address a proposed
    source. This is an illustrative way to ask questions, not a classification
    of this country or a claim that one depth is superior.
  </p>
  <p>
    Country and economy names follow the data source. Their inclusion does not
    imply a position on sovereignty or borders.
  </p>
</Entry>
<style>
  .country-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(100px, 1fr) 2fr;
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
  }
  .country-facts dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .country-facts dd {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .country-facts p {
    margin: 0.2rem 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .country-facts {
      display: block;
    }
    .country-facts dd {
      margin: 0.3rem 0 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
